# Third-party licences

`dist/calamine_wasm_bg.wasm` is a statically linked binary. The Rust crates below
are compiled into it and are redistributed as part of every published tarball,
so their licences and copyright notices ship with it.

This file is generated — run `bun run licenses` after any change to `Cargo.lock`.
CI regenerates it and fails if the result differs from what is committed.

Scope: the `wasm32-unknown-unknown` target only, so crates pulled in by `cfg`
branches that wasm never takes are excluded.

The list errs towards over-inclusion. Proc-macro crates such as `syn` and
`proc-macro2` appear even though only their *output* is linked, because Cargo
models them as ordinary dependencies and no filter separates them reliably.
Listing a crate that turned out not to ship costs a paragraph; omitting one that
did is a licence breach.

MIT appears many times below rather than once. That is deliberate: the licence
text is per-copyright-holder, and it is the copyright line that has to be
reproduced, so each distinct notice gets its own entry.

